Goku's so calm and relaxed

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.860
and pure-hearted, but obviously

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:37.560
those aren't prerequisites.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:41.930
Correct. There's more than one way to reach

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:48.470
that Goku. Reach his own.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.130
My motivation was very different than Kakarot's.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.160
My only desire was to be the

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:57.540
best, to be the greatest Saiyan alive

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:58.880
like I always had been.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:15:59.980
Until...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.620
Kakarot came along, that is.

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:07.010
But success bored like a disease inside my mind.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:11.950
For how could he be a Super Saiyan when I, the Prince of all Saiyans, could not?

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:15.460
The intensity of my training was maddening.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:21.150
Fighting with pressures of over 450 times Earth's normal gravity.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:26.090
Basic training, desperate struggle for survival.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.680
Even simplest of moves required every ounce of strength that I had.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:42.550
I wasn't sure how long I could sustain the effort without breaking in two.

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:50.590
It was as though the only thing holding my body together was my one burning desire.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.520
Be better than Kakarot.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.380
I was losing my mind.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.960
Why wasn't I able to...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:07.440
obtain what Kakarot had obtained! It didn't make any sense! It was infuriating! And it

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:15.380
was my fury that kept me alive! I decided to continue my training in the solitude of

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:20.590
space, where I would be unhindered by the distractions here on Earth. And when a violent

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:25.890
electrical storm began to blaze through the skies of the planet I was on, I welcomed it.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.980
It seemed fitting, like it was an outward manifestation of the storm.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.640
that was raging inside of me.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.360
Meteors began shooting down.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:38.290
I was determined to survive and to protect my ship from destruction.

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.740
I had a chance to get out.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.460
My only chance to get off that nightmarish heap of rubble.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.720
I thought I had it all under control.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:53.740
But then, the mother of all meteors seemed to appear out of nowhere

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:58.400
to claim my ship life.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:05.030
Normally, it would have been nothing for me to blow up that rock.

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:10.690
But after training at 450 times Earth's normal gravity for so long,

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.920
it took everything that I had and more.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.540
Then something just changed.

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:28.500
